<main class="lp-page salesroads-page" id="simple-guide">
  <div class="lp-hero-shell"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <nav class="lp-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/resources/outbound-sales-library/">Outbound Sales Library</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">CallTeam vs SalesRoads</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="lp-hero">
      <div>
        <h1>CallTeam vs <span>SalesRoads</span>
          <small>Pricing and outsourced SDRs</small>
        </h1>
        <p class="lp-intro">CallTeam starts at <strong>{{ guide.callTeamMonthly }} per month</strong> for a managed calling campaign with North America–based callers. SalesRoads starts at {{ guide.salesroadsFourWeekRate }} every four weeks for one dedicated SDR. Pay for that setup if you need a full-time rep and email outreach.</p>
        <div class="lp-actions">
          <a class="lp-button" href="#comparison">Compare the two offers <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a class="lp-text-link" href="#delivery">See how CallTeam runs a campaign <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="lp-brief salesroads-case-brief" aria-labelledby="salesroads-case-heading">
        <h2 id="salesroads-case-heading">Manufacturing campaign</h2>
        <p class="salesroads-hero-result">9 qualified appointments</p>
        <p>Booked in 90 days. Three advanced to sales opportunities.</p>
        <a href="#results">See how we got there <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div></div>

  <nav class="lp-jump" aria-label="On this page"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <a href="#comparison">Compare offers</a><a href="#pricing">Billing</a><a href="#delivery">Campaign delivery</a><a href="#results">Results</a><a href="#questions">FAQs</a>
  </div></nav>

  <section class="lp-section salesroads-first-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>What you get with each service</h2>
      <p>CallTeam offers managed calling and publishes this comparison. Prices and scope checked <time datetime="{{ guide.checkedDate }}">{{ guide.checkedLabel }}</time>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-table-wrap">
      <table class="lp-table sg-table salesroads-table" role="table">
        <caption>Service, starting price, outreach and sales handoff</caption>
        <thead><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">What to compare</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">CallTeam</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">SalesRoads</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader">What you buy</th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="CallTeam">A managed calling campaign. We can build the list or work from your accounts.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="SalesRoads">Dedicated sales development reps (SDRs) with prospect research, coaching, a strategist and campaign systems.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader">Starting price</th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="CallTeam"><strong>{{ guide.callTeamMonthly }} per month</strong> for a campaign ready to launch. Your written quote details any list research, data or extra calling coverage.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="SalesRoads"><strong>{{ guide.salesroadsFourWeekRate }} per four weeks</strong> for one SDR on its main pricing page.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader">Outreach</th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="CallTeam">North America–based callers make live calls, leave live voicemails or approved voicemail drops, and handle callbacks.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="SalesRoads">Calls and personalized email reach prospects. SalesRoads uses LinkedIn to research and verify contacts.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="row" role="rowheader">What sales receives</th>
            <td role="cell" data-label="CallTeam">A qualified appointment with the buyer’s reason to meet, current approach and agreed next step in your CRM.</td>
            <td role="cell" data-label="SalesRoads">Qualified meetings on appointment-setting plans, CRM integration and a performance dashboard.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="sg-sources"><a href="/pricing/">CallTeam pricing</a> · <a href="{{ guide.sources.salesroadsPricing.url }}">SalesRoads pricing and inclusions</a></p>
    <div class="salesroads-billing" id="pricing">
      <h3>Four-week billing means {{ guide.fourWeekPeriods }} invoices in 52 weeks</h3>
      <p>At the dedicated SDR rate, a continuous 52-week run would cost <strong>{{ guide.salesroadsYear }}</strong>. That works out to about <strong>{{ guide.salesroadsMonthlyEquivalent }} per calendar month</strong>.</p>
      <p>Ask how much rep time and email activity your quote includes. Get the invoice dates and cancellation terms in writing.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="delivery"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>How CallTeam earns a qualified meeting</h2></div>
    <div class="salesroads-process">
      <div>
        <h3>Find people with a reason to talk</h3>
        <p>Tell us what you sell and who benefits. We can research companies, find the people who own the problem and build a fresh list around that brief.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Use the call to learn what’s happening</h3>
        <p>Ask how the buyer handles the work today, where it breaks down and when they would consider a change. Their answers tell us whether to book, call later or move on.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Follow up on the buyer’s timing</h3>
        <p>If a contract renews next quarter, we ask when the buyer wants us to call. We log the date and why they asked us to follow up.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Give sales a useful opening</h3>
        <p>Your rep gets the buyer’s role, what they want to discuss and any open questions. They can start the meeting with the issue the buyer raised.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="results"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>How factory uptime led to sales conversations</h2></div>
    <div class="sg-two salesroads-proof">
      {{ processVideoPreview('See how CallTeam qualifies and follows up', 'Watch the steps from choosing accounts to briefing your salesperson.', 'callteam-vs-salesroads') }}
      <article class="salesroads-case">
        <h3>Three opportunities from nine qualified appointments</h3>
        <p>In a 90-day cybersecurity campaign, we called manufacturing leaders about downtime and recovery. One buyer entered near-term talks about changing providers. Two opportunities needed longer follow-up.</p>
        <a href="/case-studies/manufacturing-cybersecurity-appointment-setting/">Read the manufacturing cybersecurity case study <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="choose"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading">
      <h2>Compare both quotes on the same work</h2>
      <p>Give both providers the same buyer profile and ask for the full price, including any data and setup fees. Once the campaign runs, divide that spend by the meetings that took place and met your criteria.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-mid-cta">
      <p><strong>Want CallTeam to take this on?</strong> Bring your offer and target market. We’ll map the list, calling and follow-up you need.</p>
      <a class="lp-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-booking-placement="callteam-vs-salesroads">Book a free 30-minute call <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <p class="salesroads-next-step"><a href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/">See how we’d run your campaign <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="questions"><div class="lp-wrap lp-faq-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>CallTeam vs SalesRoads FAQs</h2></div>
    <div class="lp-faqs">{% for faq in guide.faqs %}<details><summary>{{ faq.question }}</summary><p>{{ faq.answer }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper salesroads-sources" id="sources"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>Sources</h2></div>
    <ul>{% for key, source in guide.sources %}<li><a href="{{ source.url }}">{{ source.label }}</a></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    <p>For more options, see the <a href="/resources/b2b-lead-generation-pricing-report/">B2B lead generation pricing report</a>.</p>
    <p>Comparing the two agencies directly? Read <a href="/compare/belkins-vs-salesroads/">Belkins vs SalesRoads</a>.</p>
  </div></section>
</main>
